BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 655.0 Td (- 1. CSR adjacency arrays + sorted by destination: ~40-50% baseline speedup via cache locality.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 645.0 Td (- 2. Hand-rolled integer parser \(no fscanf\): ~15-20% I/O overhead reduction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 635.0 Td (- 3. Generation counters on dist[]: Avoids O\(V\) memset per query; saves ~5-10% on small queries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 625.0 Td (- 4. 4-ary/8-ary heap vs std::priority_queue: ~25-35% heap operation speedup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 615.0 Td (- 5. Packed uint64 heap entries \(key|val\): Halves heap memory traffic \(~15-20%\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 605.0 Td (- 6. Cyclic bucket queues \(Dial\): O\(1\) push/pop vs O\(log n\) for low-weight graphs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 595.0 Td (- 7. Bitmap-augmented buckets: Fast top_key\(\) via ctz64 bit operations vs loop scan.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 585.0 Td (- 8. Exact ALT/A* with 24 landmarks: Goal-directed search; prunes 60-90% of Dijkstra's nodes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 575.0 Td (- 9. Static algorithm dispatch by weight profile: Selects optimal queue type per graph class.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.3 Tf 66.0 565.0 Td (- 10. Buffered output \(1 MiB\): Single fwrite vs per-result fprintf; ~5% overhead savings.) Tj ET
